  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Dryad dataset shows active use, with 3,224 downloads and 4,655 views, alongside an early but real scholarly footprint of 3 citations and 3 documented downstream reuses. The record suggests sustained access and some reuse beyond the original publication, while the citation base remains small.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest signal for this dataset is use: it has been downloaded 3,224 times and viewed 4,655 times, indicating continued interest in the underlying material. It is also linked to the related article in BMJ Open, which helps situate the dataset as part of a published research workflow rather than a standalone archive item.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Scholarly uptake is present but still modest. OpenAlex records 3 citations, all in article-form publications, with citations appearing in 2014 and 2021. That pattern points to a limited but continuing research presence rather than a large citation burst concentrated immediately after release.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The reuse record adds an important nuance: 3 downstream reuses are documented, again all in articles. This indicates that the dataset has been incorporated into later scholarly work, even though the available record does not show a broad or highly diversified reuse network.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the evidence supports a narrative of an accessible, actively consulted dataset with early-stage scholarly influence. The impact profile is driven more by usage and a small number of documented reuses than by a large citation count, so the record is best read as emerging rather than mature impact.</p>",
